    a: "Because levered cash flow measures the cash the owners can take out, and principal leaves the property's bank account just like interest. It isn't an expense because you don't lose it: it pays down the loan, so you get it back as a smaller payoff when you sell or refinance. Equity returns capture that through higher net sale proceeds.",
